# The looting party at the survey gallery mouth (crypt surface map).
# Auto-opens when a colonist gets near the captain (MapComponent_TSC_
# CryptParley). Every exit resolves the group: parley_hostile = the crew
# turns bandit and attacks; parley_flee = the Arcana 10 scare sends them
# running. One encounter per save (TSC_CryptBanditsMet).

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_CryptBandits

== start ==
There are armed men at the gallery mouth, and they have brought picks and shovels as well as blades. Their captain steps out to meet you.

"More diggers," he says. "No. This hole is claimed, friends. Everything in it is spoken for. Walk away and keep your boots."

* "Feel the air coming out of that hole. The magic below is unstable. Dig, and you won't come back up."
    check Arcana 10 -> scared | called_bluff
    on success do parley_flee()
    on fail do parley_hostile()
* "It's claimed, all right. By the Wayfarers' Guild. Draw or walk." -> fight
    do parley_hostile()
* [Say nothing. Draw steel.] -> fight
    do parley_hostile()

== scared ==
The captain's eyes go to the gallery mouth. The air rising out of it is warm, and it should not be, and every man behind him knows it.

"Told you this hole smelled wrong," someone mutters.

"Keep it," the captain says. "Dig your own graves." They go, and they do not look back.

* [Watch them leave.] -> end

== called_bluff ==
"Unstable magic." The captain smiles. "I've heard better from fortune tellers at half the price. The only thing unstable here is your odds. Take them."

* [Steel.] -> end

== fight ==
"Wrong answer," the captain says, and the picks come down and the blades come out.

* [Steel.] -> end
